h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 544)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Double-click the eraser to clear the frame.</b> The first click still picks the tool. The same gesture works in the web review.</li>
<li><b>Stopping on a frame in a browser shows that frame at full resolution.</b> The streamed picture is encoded for movement; park on a frame and the exact frame arrives over it, full size and in the clip's own color, for as long as you stay there.</li>
<li><b>Reviews shared to the web are lighter and play sooner</b> — the picture is capped at 1920 on its long edge, so a 4K or 4.6K plate no longer encodes at a size no connection can stream, and the page buffers ahead and caches as it goes.</li>
<li><b>The web review has zoom shortcuts, full screen and a foldaway notes panel.</b> F or 0 fits, 1 / 2 / 3 / 4 zoom, + and − step, ⇧F fills the display, N folds the notes away.</li>
<li><b>Fixed: the web display-gamma menu appeared to do nothing</b> on a paused frame, which is exactly when it matters.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
