h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 537)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Reviews shared to the web play smoothly.</b> The picture people open in a browser is a quarter of the weight it was and streams in the band Frame.io and Vimeo use, and the page now buffers twenty seconds ahead and caches the clip as it goes instead of fetching a few seconds at a time.</li>
<li><b>The web review fits a scaled window.</b> On a 14" screen with the window not full, the transport and markup controls ran off the ends of the bar. It wraps now, with nothing off-screen.</li>
<li><b>The web playlist is findable</b> — the header line that says which clip you're on opens it.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
